    "summary": "Acoustic gems, fierce electric jams, stellar soundboard",
    "blurb": "Features two acoustic sets bookending a New Riders interlude and two electric halves, with standout performances of 'Friend Of The Devil', 'Candyman' and an expansive 'Dark Star'. Jerry’s guitar is fierce throughout, Phil provides thunderous bass on the jams, and Pigpen adds organ fire. The pristine soundboard capture offers crystal‑clear audio despite minor tape glitches.",
    "review": "On May 15, 1970 at the Fillmore East the Dead delivered a marathon that still feels like a single, seamless narrative. The early acoustic set opened with folk‑tight numbers such as \"Friend Of The Devil\" and \"Candyman\", then gave way to a New Riders of the Purple Sage interlude before diving into two electric halves packed with monster jams – a soaring \"Dark Star\", double‑take on \"Good Lovin'\", and a rousing finale with \"Cold Jordan*\". Jerry Garcia was in top form, his guitar ranging from sweet pedal‑steel sweetness on the acoustic numbers to fierce, searing leads on the electric stretches; Phil Lesh’s bass rolled thunderously under the improvisations, while Pigpen’s organ and gritty vocals added fire to the middle of the show. Bill Kreutzmann’s extensive drum solo in the first electric half injected swing into \"Dark Star\", and Mickey Hart’s subtle brush work kept the acoustic numbers breathing. The soundboard recording (gd70-05-15.early-late.sbd.97.sbeok.shnf) captures this brilliance with crystal‑clear highs, tight lows and superb instrument separation, making it the definitive way to experience one of 1970’s most legendary Fillmore nights.",
